From f0170130c9a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yong.wang
Date: Mon Nov 03 16:19:02 2025 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: Fix shrink_many UAF of memcg

ANDROID: Fix shrink_many UAF of memcg

shrink_many() released memcg before should_abort_scan() dereferenced
lruvec. When that was the last reference the memcg (and its lruvec) was
freed, giving a KASAN use-after-free in should_abort_scan() from kswapd.

Reset lruvec at the restart label and put memcg only after the abort
check is done.

Source: AOSP android14-6.1-lts f0170130c9a7
---
diff --git a/mm/vmscan.c b/mm/vmscan.c
index 30c8013e..486b324 100644
--- a/mm/vmscan.c
+++ b/mm/vmscan.c
@@ -5507,6 +5507,7 @@ static void shrink_many(struct pglist_data *pgdat, struct scan_control *sc)
 	bin = first_bin = get_random_u32_below(MEMCG_NR_BINS);
 restart:
 	op = 0;
+	lruvec = NULL;
 	memcg = NULL;
 	gen = get_memcg_gen(READ_ONCE(pgdat->memcg_lru.seq));
 
@@ -5548,10 +5549,12 @@ static void shrink_many(struct pglist_data *pgdat, struct scan_control *sc)
 	if (op)
 		lru_gen_rotate_memcg(lruvec, op);
 
-	mem_cgroup_put(memcg);
-
-	if (lruvec && should_abort_scan(lruvec, sc))
+	if (lruvec && should_abort_scan(lruvec, sc)) {
+		mem_cgroup_put(memcg);
 		return;
+	}
+
+	mem_cgroup_put(memcg);
 
 	/* restart if raced with lru_gen_rotate_memcg() */
 	if (gen != get_nulls_value(pos))
